## General eligibility criteria for CAP/DA

Under **Clinical Coverage Policy 3K-2, Section 3.2.1** (`sec:doc:clinical_policy:3K-2:3.2.1`), Medicaid covers CAP/DA when the beneficiary:

- **Meets the required HCBS nursing facility level of care (LOC)** as determined by NC Medicaid and needs long-term care support at a level typically provided in an institution, based on a documented medical diagnosis and functional care need, as assessed quarterly;
- Has a CAP assessment showing a **reasonable indication** that the person would need a service plan for at least one CAP/DA HCBS within **30 calendar days** of evaluation;
- Has a **signed service plan** authorizing one or more waiver services on a monthly basis to help avoid institutionalization through coordinated case management;
- Has a signed service plan authorizing installation of equipment, modification, or technology on a short-term basis to return to or remain in the primary private residence and prevent institutional placement;
- Is **able to maintain health, safety, and well-being** at the primary private residence or approved location using formal and informal supports;
- Has **paid care needs** that can be maintained within the **average institutional cost** of the CAP/DA waiver;
- Has a **primary physician** who can link and coordinate all medical services; and
- Has an **emergency back-up and disaster plan** for when caregivers cannot provide services or during emergencies like weather events or pandemics.

## Additional criteria for Consumer-Directed services

The same section says CAP/DA **Consumer-Directed services** are covered only if the beneficiary meets **all of the above** plus:

- Understands the rights and responsibilities of directing their own care, shown by completing the required self-assessment questionnaire and introductory consumer direction training/orientation;
- Is willing and emotionally capable of acting as an employer/director of care, or selects a representative who is willing and capable;
- Meets the criteria in **Subsection 3.2.2(a) and (b)**; and
- Has an approved service plan identifying the amount, duration, frequency, and NPI of CAP/DA and non-CAP/DA services, follows all policy/legal requirements, and signs Beneficiary Rights and Responsibilities.

### Citation
- **Clinical Coverage Policy 3K-2, Section 3.2.1** (`sec:doc:clinical_policy:3K-2:3.2.1`), no amendments found.

